{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162562-i-was-a-dogwood-in-another-life-contemplating-spiritual-ontology","id":162562,"title":"I Was A Dogwood In Another Life - Contemplating Spiritual Ontology","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-08T11:28:45-07:00","id":162562,"title":"I Was A Dogwood In Another Life - Contemplating Spiritual Ontology","content":"Idle theory that I'd like to get some impressions on: suppose spirits &quot;came from&quot; the reincarnation of humans (or other antediluvian/alien things that could leave ghosts), subjected to the usually-postulated erasure of memory the dead undergo when they're reborn. It's conveniently unprovable within the scope of commonly-held metaphysics, but I was wondering if anybody cared to offer any thoughts on the notion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T17:25:33-07:00","id":162977,"title":"","content":"Seems like something that'd raise more questions than answers. I mean, basically everything that exists has a spirit though most of them are dormant, so where exactly did all those souls come from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:48:43-07:00","id":163045,"title":"","content":"Well, you could turn it the otherway and propose a Theosophy-like theory that souls are evolved spirits. Which stills leaves the mechanism on how that works up in the air.<br /> <br /> Step 1: Evolve<br /> Step 2: ???<br /> Step 3: Souls!<br /> <br /> As for spirits being... well, souls, mmmm. Well, you'd have to excise the bit about spirits spontaneously generating, which makes spirits more rare. Then you'd have to figure out how a person goes from ghost -&gt; spirit. Especially things like Animal spirits. Does that mean Father/Mother Wolf was human once? How about Luna? I guess it would mean that there are no spirits where there isn't soul'd life, mm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T19:01:05-07:00","id":163054,"title":"","content":"General bit of course-correction to account for what seems to be one data point away from a consistent misapprehension: I'm not suggesting spirits are souls. There's no problem of resource shortage, given one can theoretically encounter multiple ghosts who are all reincarnations of the same person without making a claim that that person had multiple souls.<br /> <br /> I'm suggesting the bits of cognition that make up the aggregate consciousnesses of spirits come from the bits of cognition that used to make up the aggregate consciousnesses of the classes of being that do not (any longer?) have reflections in the Shadow, those being (in the World of Darkness in its current known state) sapient entities who are mostly capable of forming ghosts with their death.<br /> <br /> In short, assuming that ghosts are a byproduct of the death of ensouled beings, the theory goes that spirits are what happens to some percentage of ghosts when they pass on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T19:04:50-07:00","id":163057,"title":"","content":"I see.<br /> <br /> Well, I don't see it -not- working. It gives a different flavor to the setting, and for the Uratha to be half-spirit. It'd have an impact on some of the ways one deals with ghosts and spirits. I'd be tempted to say, if you do that, make the Underworld and the Shadow one realm, and have ghosts who make it to the surface being the ones who turn into spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T19:09:14-07:00","id":163058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162562-i-was-a-dogwood-in-another-life-contemplating-spiritual-ontology?p=163054#post163054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, assuming that ghosts are a byproduct of the death of ensouled beings, the theory goes that spirits are what happens to some percentage of ghosts when they pass on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing that Giests are midway through this process?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T21:04:33-07:00","id":163110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162562-i-was-a-dogwood-in-another-life-contemplating-spiritual-ontology?p=163057#post163057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see.<br /> <br /> Well, I don't see it -not- working.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I meant by &quot;conveniently unprovable.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It gives a different flavor to the setting, and for the Uratha to be half-spirit. </div> </div> </div>That it does, and in fact that was one of the things I hoped might see some discussion. Suppose it casts the Uratha's status as &quot;born of exile&quot; in a curious light.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It'd have an impact on some of the ways one deals with ghosts and spirits. I'd be tempted to say, if you do that, make the Underworld and the Shadow one realm, and have ghosts who make it to the surface being the ones who turn into spirits. </div> </div> </div>I'm of the opinion that the bits of Werewolf, Mage, et al, that refer to the Underworld as though it were a particularly deep portion of the Shadow aren't entirely in error, and there seems to be a rather more open level of connection and transit between those two realms relative to the rest of the better-known cosmology, but the mechanism I'm postulating isn't quite as prosaic as &quot;put a ghost in the Shadow until it goes native.&quot; It's more like:<br /> <br /> Human dies &gt; Ghost is formed &gt; Stuff Happens &gt; Ghost passes on, abandoning its ghostly-ephemeral Corpus and attendant memories and possibly breaking up into fragmentary consciousnesses &gt; Ghost's mind or pieces thereof go through Nebulous Otherworldly Channels &gt; Cognitive elements form the basis of an &quot;appropriate&quot; new spirit with no conscious awareness of its former life.<br /> <br /> With a side order of:<br /> <br /> Spirit is permanently destroyed &gt; [hypothetical stopover in the Underworld as one of the many sorts of Anomaly, as suggested by Second Sight's section on spirits and ghosts and &quot;crossover&quot; between the two?] &gt; Spirit's fragmentary mind is recycled into the bases for other spirits, who repeat the process when they &quot;die&quot; ad infinitum barring escape valves.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's chiefly a means of emphasizing that the cosmology of the nWoD is difficult to track and that one can never be entirely sure where they stand in dealing with spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162562-i-was-a-dogwood-in-another-life-contemplating-spiritual-ontology?p=163058#post163058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing that Giests are midway through this process?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather the opposite; geister in general are <i>more</i> entwined with the workings of the Underworld - they've become merged with aspects of a nigh-infinite Mystery and tend to be that much harder to resolve as a consequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T22:26:01-07:00","id":163173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162562-i-was-a-dogwood-in-another-life-contemplating-spiritual-ontology?p=163110#post163110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b...It's chiefly a means of emphasizing that the cosmology of the nWoD is difficult to track and that one can never be entirely sure where they stand in dealing with spirits.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>That, my friend, is something WoD does very well. I'm inclined, in my own game, to make it even more of a clusterfuck. Some spirits are born from the fragments of ghosts, and other's are born from ambient Essence that germinates. <br /> <br /> However, making the Shadow and Underworld closer to one another has an interesting effect of cementing that the Essence both use are the same thing, just with different resonances. (I've always wondered if that's answered canonically. If spirits, ghosts and angels use the same fuel source, and if so, what is Essence really?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T23:13:03-07:00","id":176770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162562-i-was-a-dogwood-in-another-life-contemplating-spiritual-ontology?p=163173#post163173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, my friend, is something WoD does very well. I'm inclined, in my own game, to make it even more of a clusterfuck. Some spirits are born from the fragments of ghosts, and <b>other's are born from ambient Essence that germinates.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be the &quot;side order&quot; I mentioned.<br /> <br /> I can't help but wonder if the Supernumeraries changelings encounter in dreams might run on a more temporary version of those Nebulous Otherworldly Channels - short-term adoption of roles in a dream whose script you know seems loosely comparable to long-term adoption of a particular class of ephemera (and now I'm remembering Geist's sample krewe member who thought of death as a stance on existence) that can, with the right Numen, get a glimpse of the future.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, making the Shadow and Underworld closer to one another has an interesting effect of cementing that the Essence both use are the same thing, just with different resonances. (I've always wondered if that's answered canonically. If spirits, ghosts and angels use the same fuel source, and if so, what is Essence really?) </div> </div> </div>If we take the GMC appendix's description at face value, it's an energy the comes from emotion and memory \u2014 the Shadow near Earth is shaped by the active flows of Essence from the memory of the surrounding landscape, adjusted for perception-based distortion from sentient (though not necessarily sapient) observers, and Book of the Dead's writeup of Oppia makes note of the Essence produced by the remembrance of the dead.<br /> <br /> Astral beings running on Essence is pointed out as a metaphysical curiousity in Astral Realms, and one can probably assume that angels regaining Essence from sacrifice (presumably the Essence generated is drawing on the memory of the destroyed object or creature) has something to do with the Machine's more sterile modus operandi; I've thought that Glamour being called out as sort of between Mana and Glamour in qualities seemed to link up nicely to the &quot;lapsed mechanical stewards of Fate&quot; origin story for the True Fae, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T23:38:49-07:00","id":176785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162562-i-was-a-dogwood-in-another-life-contemplating-spiritual-ontology?p=163173#post163173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, my friend, is something WoD does very well. I'm inclined, in my own game, to make it even more of a clusterfuck. Some spirits are born from the fragments of ghosts, and other's are born from ambient Essence that germinates.<br /> <br /> However, making the Shadow and Underworld closer to one another has an interesting effect of cementing that the Essence both use are the same thing, just with different resonances. (I've always wondered if that's answered canonically. If spirits, ghosts and angels use the same fuel source, and if so, what is Essence really?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well actually that has been answered.<br /> <br /> The essences are different flavored, but still fundamentally the same thing:<br /> <br /> Idigam can manipulate the essence of both spirits and ghosts.<br /> <br /> Ephemerals can buy the essence eater numina that allows them to eat any kind of essence<br /> <br /> Ghosts trapped in the hisil eat hisil essence and become spirit like.<br /> <br /> Spirits that eat ghosts can become ghost-spirit magath.<br /> <br /> Demons can craft ghost plasm into a spirit suit and vice versa.<br /> <br /> Werewolves can eat ghosts to gain essence.<br /> <br /> The strix can gain a power to enter the gauntlet and sup from spirits and ghosts.<br /> <br /> Bloody Mary may be a ghost that gained a spirit like state as an urban legend.<br /> <br /> And the loa may include spirits that used to be ghosts, and ghosts that used to be spirits. <br /> <br /> If the ephemerals were meant to be fundamentally different it wouldn't make sense for a ghost to be able to attack an angel for essence, just for that angel to fall and then use an exploit to attack that ghost so they can later make a fire spirit cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}